    {
     "type": "code",
     "head": "Prune with a sorted break",
     "say": "Same skeleton. Left is what we still need. Zero left means a full answer: save it. Now the prune. The list is sorted, so a candidate bigger than left means every later one is too. Break. Passing j, not j plus one, lets a number repeat.",
     "panels": [
      {
       "file": "sol.cpp",
       "code": "// a is sorted; numbers may be reused\nvoid comb(vector<int>& a, int i, int left,\n          vector<int>& cur, vector<vector<int>>& out) {\n    if (left == 0) { out.push_back(cur); return; }\n    for (int j = i; j < (int)a.size(); j++) {\n        if (a[j] > left) break;\n        cur.push_back(a[j]);\n        comb(a, j, left - a[j], cur, out);\n        cur.pop_back();\n    }\n}"
      }
     ],
     "steps": [
